{"schema_version":1,"task_id":"code-6261fff562f42807","paper_id":"2208.04654v1","variant":"original","kind":"code","outcome":"checked","reason":null,"error":null,"findings":[{"finding_id":"code-6261fff562f42807-f0","task_id":"code-6261fff562f42807","paper_id":"2208.04654v1","variant":"original","error_class":"method_mismatch","anchor":{"kind":"document"},"target":{"kind":"setting","key":"method"},"summary":"In cfg.py, t60_range is set to [0.2, 0.4, 0.6], omitting 0.8 s and 1.0 s from the evaluation grid.","explanation":"Evaluation discrepancy, high confidence.","evidence":[{"kind":"quote","source":{"kind":"submission","id":"2208.04654v1","title":null,"url":null},"text":"Each recording was evaluated for SNRs ∈ {0, 6, 12, 18, 24, 30} dB and reverberation times T60 ∈ {0.2, 0.4, 0.6, 0.8, 1} s.","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":null,"line_start":null,"line_end":null},{"kind":"code","source":{"kind":"repository","id":"https://github.com/axeber01/ngcc@2210bf55395669c1c39d49f65f286fc9a1523fc9","title":null,"url":"https://github.com/axeber01/ngcc"},"text":"snr_range = [0, 6, 12, 18, 24, 30]\nt60_range = [0.2, 0.4, 0.6]","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":"cfg.py","line_start":27,"line_end":28}],"uncertain":false},{"finding_id":"code-6261fff562f42807-f1","task_id":"code-6261fff562f42807","paper_id":"2208.04654v1","variant":"original","error_class":"method_mismatch","anchor":{"kind":"document"},"target":{"kind":"setting","key":"method"},"summary":"The network g_theta outputs unnormalized raw logits directly from final_conv without applying softmax normalization in the final layer.","explanation":"Model discrepancy, high confidence.","evidence":[{"kind":"quote","source":{"kind":"submission","id":"2208.04654v1","title":null,"url":null},"text":"In order to output a probability distribution over time shifts, the GCC-PHAT output is fed into another network g θ : R (2τmax+1)×L → R (2τmax+1) , with its own set of parameters θ that combines the L different correlations and applies softmax normalization in the final layer.","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":null,"line_start":null,"line_end":null},{"kind":"code","source":{"kind":"repository","id":"https://github.com/axeber01/ngcc@2210bf55395669c1c39d49f65f286fc9a1523fc9","title":null,"url":"https://github.com/axeber01/ngcc"},"text":"        s = cc.shape[2]\n        padding = get_pad(\n            size=s, kernel_size=self.final_kernel, stride=1, dilation=1)\n        cc = F.pad(cc, pad=padding, mode='constant')\n        cc = self.final_conv(cc).reshape([batch_size, -1])","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":"model.py","line_start":151,"line_end":155}],"uncertain":false},{"finding_id":"code-6261fff562f42807-f2","task_id":"code-6261fff562f42807","paper_id":"2208.04654v1","variant":"original","error_class":"method_mismatch","anchor":{"kind":"document"},"target":{"kind":"setting","key":"method"},"summary":"The hidden layers of g_theta include Dropout(0.5) following LeakyReLU, which is not part of the model architecture described in the paper.","explanation":"Model discrepancy, high confidence.","evidence":[{"kind":"quote","source":{"kind":"submission","id":"2208.04654v1","title":null,"url":null},"text":"Similarly, g θ consists of 4 convolutional layers with filters of length 11, 9, 7 and 5, all of which has 128 output channels, except for the last layer that has a single output channel which models the log-probabilities for each time delay.","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":null,"line_start":null,"line_end":null},{"kind":"code","source":{"kind":"repository","id":"https://github.com/axeber01/ngcc@2210bf55395669c1c39d49f65f286fc9a1523fc9","title":null,"url":"https://github.com/axeber01/ngcc"},"text":"        self.mlp = nn.ModuleList([nn.Sequential(\n                nn.Conv1d(self.channels[i], self.channels[i+1], kernel_size=k),\n                nn.BatchNorm1d(self.channels[i+1]),\n                nn.LeakyReLU(0.2),\n                nn.Dropout(0.5)) for i, k in enumerate(self.mlp_kernels)])","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":"model.py","line_start":121,"line_end":125}],"uncertain":false},{"finding_id":"code-6261fff562f42807-f3","task_id":"code-6261fff562f42807","paper_id":"2208.04654v1","variant":"original","error_class":"method_mismatch","anchor":{"kind":"document"},"target":{"kind":"setting","key":"method"},"summary":"The dataset is loaded from LibriSpeech test-clean (which has 40 speakers in total); reserving 3 speakers for validation and 3 for testing leaves 34 speakers for training rather than 40.","explanation":"Data discrepancy, high confidence.","evidence":[{"kind":"quote","source":{"kind":"submission","id":"2208.04654v1","title":null,"url":null},"text":"We split the data based on speakers, such that 40 speakers were used for training, 3 for validation and 3 for testing.","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":null,"line_start":null,"line_end":null},{"kind":"code","source":{"kind":"repository","id":"https://github.com/axeber01/ngcc@2210bf55395669c1c39d49f65f286fc9a1523fc9","title":null,"url":"https://github.com/axeber01/ngcc"},"text":"indices_test = [i for i, ((waveform, sample_rate, transcript, speaker_id, utterance_number), pos, seed)\n                in enumerate(train_set) if speaker_id in TEST_IDS]\nindices_val = [i for i, ((waveform, sample_rate, transcript, speaker_id, utterance_number), pos, seed)\n               in enumerate(train_set) if speaker_id in VAL_IDS]\nindices_train = [i for i, ((waveform, sample_rate, transcript, speaker_id, utterance_number), pos, seed)\n                 in enumerate(train_set) if speaker_id not in TEST_IDS and speaker_id not in VAL_IDS]\n\ntrain_set = data_utils.Subset(train_set, indices_train)","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":"main.py","line_start":99,"line_end":106}],"uncertain":false}],"attempts":1}
